<article> <header class="hero"> <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"> <a href="/">Home</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <a href="/glossary">Glossary</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <span>ISO 20022 XML schema (postal address)</span> </nav> <div class="hero-badge"><span class="pulse-dot"></span><span style="position:relative;z-index:1">Glossary · Messages</span></div> <h1><span class="accent">ISO 20022 XML schema (postal address)</span></h1> <p class="page-meta">Glossary entry · Last reviewed 26 July 2026</p> <!-- ANSWER BLOCK — picked up by speakable schema --> <p class="answer-block">The <strong>ISO 20022 XML schema</strong> (XSD) for postal addresses defines the <code>&lt;PstlAdr&gt;</code> container and its child elements with exact types and lengths: <code>&lt;TwnNm&gt;</code> up to 35 characters, <code>&lt;StrtNm&gt;</code> 70, <code>&lt;BldgNb&gt;</code> 16, <code>&lt;PstCd&gt;</code> 16, <code>&lt;Ctry&gt;</code> as <code>[A-Z]&#123;2&#125;</code>, and <code>&lt;AdrLine&gt;</code> at 70 characters per occurrence with format-dependent cardinality.</p> </header> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">In Practice</div> <h2 class="section-title">How ISO 20022 XML schema (postal address) works in practice</h2> <div class="content-block"><p>Parsers should validate against the XSD and then apply the format rules the schema alone cannot express: <code>&lt;AdrLine&gt;</code> cardinality of 0 in fully structured, [0..2] in hybrid and up to 7 in the decommissioned unstructured format, plus the No-Duplication Rule between structured elements and address lines.</p></div> <p class="src">Source: the ioNova Postal Address Specification v2.0 §3.2 (element table) and §3.4.3 (Figure 2 — XML schema structure); CPMI harmonisation requirements — technical annex §0.13–§0.31 / p5.</p> <div class="content-block"><p>The schema skeleton with types, lengths and cardinality notes:</p></div>
<div class="code-block"><pre><span class="tag">&lt;PstlAdr&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;Dept&gt;</span>text&#123;1,70&#125;<span class="tag">&lt;/Dept&gt;</span>            <span class="tag">&lt;SubDept&gt;</span>text&#123;1,70&#125;<span class="tag">&lt;/SubDept&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;StrtNm&gt;</span>text&#123;1,70&#125;<span class="tag">&lt;/StrtNm&gt;</span>        <span class="tag">&lt;BldgNb&gt;</span>text&#123;1,16&#125;<span class="tag">&lt;/BldgNb&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;BldgNm&gt;</span>text&#123;1,35&#125;<span class="tag">&lt;/BldgNm&gt;</span>        <span class="tag">&lt;Flr&gt;</span>text&#123;1,70&#125;<span class="tag">&lt;/Flr&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;PstBx&gt;</span>text&#123;1,16&#125;<span class="tag">&lt;/PstBx&gt;</span>          <span class="tag">&lt;Room&gt;</span>text&#123;1,70&#125;<span class="tag">&lt;/Room&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;PstCd&gt;</span>text&#123;1,16&#125;<span class="tag">&lt;/PstCd&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;TwnNm&gt;</span>text&#123;1,35&#125;<span class="tag">&lt;/TwnNm&gt;</span>          <span class="cmt">&lt;!-- MANDATORY --&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;TwnLctnNm&gt;</span>text&#123;1,35&#125;<span class="tag">&lt;/TwnLctnNm&gt;</span>  <span class="tag">&lt;DstrctNm&gt;</span>text&#123;1,35&#125;<span class="tag">&lt;/DstrctNm&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;CtrySubDvsn&gt;</span>text&#123;1,35&#125;<span class="tag">&lt;/CtrySubDvsn&gt;</span>  <span class="cmt">&lt;!-- ISO 3166-2 --&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;Ctry&gt;</span>[A-Z]&#123;2&#125;<span class="tag">&lt;/Ctry&gt;</span>              <span class="cmt">&lt;!-- MANDATORY --&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;AdrLine&gt;</span>text&#123;1,70&#125;<span class="tag">&lt;/AdrLine&gt;</span>      <span class="cmt">&lt;!-- 0 structured / [0..2] hybrid / [0..7] unstructured --&gt;</span>
<span class="tag">&lt;/PstlAdr&gt;</span></pre></div> <div class="content-block"><p>Parent reference: <a href="/address-intelligence/structured-address-mandate">ISO 20022 structured address mandate</a>.</p></div> </section> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">Citations</div> <h2 class="section-title">Sources</h2> <div class="sources-list"> <h3 class="sources-subhead">Standards &amp; regulatory sources</h3>
